    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["Q1", "J1", "J2"],
      "pins": ["Q1.3", "J1.29", "J2.29"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Net-(J5-Pin_1)"],
      "observed": "The netlist places Q1 pin 3 (D) on the GND net, and J1/J2 pin 29 are also on GND; Q1 pin 2 (S) is on Net-(J5-Pin_1). There is no /BAT net connecting the battery switch to the M5Stack bus.",
      "expected": "Q1 should connect the battery connector to a /BAT net, and that /BAT net should go to the M5Stack bus BAT pin (spec: pin 29), not to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"30\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"29\") (pinfunction \"Pin_29\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"29\") (pinfunction \"Pin_29\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"Net-(J5-Pin_1)\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Q1 ... gates the battery connector (J5) onto the `/BAT` bus net."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "onto the `/BAT` net, which is wired straight to pin 29 of the M5Stack bus connectors"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The M5Stack BAT/charging rail is not connected to the battery; when SW1 closes, Q1 turns on and connects the battery source directly to GND, creating a short and likely damaging the board or preventing battery operation.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The PWM/serial jumper network and 5V diode path match the specification, but the battery switch is miswired: Q1's drain and the intended BAT bus pin are tied to GND instead of a /BAT net, shorting the battery path and disabling the M5Stack battery/charging connection."
}

